     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is twice the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me which option you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
